confconsole (2.2.3+keel5) trixie; urgency=low

  * Database mode, Cloud / Primary: once the primary is configured, the
    screen shows what each replica's screen asks for: the addresses to
    replicate from, IPv6 first, the port, the replication account keel
    names (repl) and the file that holds its password. A primary that
    answers on loopback only is offered this node's own addresses in the
    form, every stable one and public before unique local (the usage
    screen's single pick per interface was the fd00:: one on a test VM),
    and one nobody can reach says so instead of handing out ::1.
  * Cloud / Primary: when the password file holds nothing, offer to
    generate a password, write it root only (0600, directory 0700) and
    show it once, after the apply, to paste into each replica. A file that
    already holds one is kept and never shown or regenerated, because the
    replicas configured with it would stop authenticating.
  * Cloud / Replica: ask for the replication password itself, hidden, and
    write it to the file the description references, instead of asking the
    operator for a file to create by hand. A blank keeps the file's value.
  * Cloud / Replica: warn before anything is changed that becoming a
    replica replaces the data on this node with a copy of the primary; No
    leaves the description, the secret and the server as they were. keel's
    own refusal is still asked separately before --destroy-local-database.
  * The password is written after keel spec validate accepted the new
    description and before it is committed and applied, so a refused
    description leaves no credential behind and the apply never runs
    without it.

 -- Marcos Méndez <mendez.foto@gmail.com>  Wed, 30 Sep 2026 12:00:00 +0000

confconsole (2.2.3+keel4) trixie; urgency=low

  * Usage screen: centre the mark above it. It was prepended as it was read,
    so it sat against the left edge of the dialog; the whole block is now
    shifted by one indent, measured from its widest line, on the same width
    the mark is admitted on.
  * keelbanner: take the mark's size from the installed files instead of
    stating it, so the overlay can redraw the art without a change here.

 -- Keel Linux maintainers <admin@keellinux.org>  Sun, 27 Sep 2026 18:00:06 +0000

confconsole (2.2.3+keel3) trixie; urgency=low

  * Instance menu: add Database mode, the console half of handbook decision
    0013. Standalone, or Cloud splitting into Primary and Replica, each
    leading to a screen that configures THIS node and nothing else: the
    addresses it answers on, the origins a primary allows to replicate from
    it, the endpoint a replica replicates from, and the file holding the
    replication credential. A prefix is offered as the form to prefer and a
    name is called fragile, which is what docs/spec.md of keel says.
  * Every cloud screen states, in a line the operator cannot miss, that this
    replication has no automatic failover: if the primary stops, nothing
    takes over by itself.
  * Promote this replica is its own entry, and asks first, because promoting
    while the old primary still runs leaves two writable servers holding one
    dataset. It says so in the question.
  * Becoming a replica replaces the local database. The screen never decides
    that: it shows keel's own refusal and asks whether to go on, and only a
    Yes adds --destroy-local-database to the run.
  * What the operator typed is staged beside the description and handed to
    keel spec validate before it replaces it, so a value that would not load
    cannot replace one that does.
  * Depend on python3-yaml: the menu writes the description it collected.

 -- Marcos Méndez <mendez.foto@gmail.com>  Sun, 27 Sep 2026 15:50:00 +0000

confconsole (2.2.3+keel2) trixie; urgency=low

  * Add the Instance menu: view the instance description, apply it, show the
    drift between it and the machine, and export what the machine says as a
    description. The menu is a front end over the keel client (keelcli), so
    the console and the command line answer from the same code.
  * Usage screen: put the mark above it, dropping to the small mark and then
    to none before the addresses lose a line, so a serial console and an
    80x24 terminal both render it.
  * Recommend keel rather than suggest it: the Instance menu calls it, and
    without it the menu says so instead of failing, so it stays a
    recommendation and the package remains installable on its own.

 -- Keel Linux maintainers <admin@keellinux.org>  Sat, 26 Sep 2026 22:03:04 +0000

confconsole (2.2.3+keel1) trixie; urgency=low

  * ifutil: add the static IPv6 writer, NetworkInterfaces.set_static6 and
    set_dhcp6 with the module wrappers set_static6, set_dhcp6 and get_ip6conf;
    get_ipv6conf prefers a stable address over a temporary one.
  * Networking menu: add the Static IPv6 entry (address/prefix, gateway,
    name server), clearing every field restores inet6 dhcp.
  * Usage screen: show IPv6 first, on the screen and in the adapter list.
  * Add the tests: pytest for ifutil and the dialogs, with coverage checked
    on every pull request.

